  "term": "Golden Rule",
  "definition": "The Golden Rule is the Gospel precept that a person should treat others as they would want others to treat them. In moral and social thought, it has often been taken as a brief statement of social morality, and it is broader than the merely negative idea of simply avoiding harm to others.",
